svg_text:
The life cycle of corn | A maize sporophyte has a tassel and an ear shoot. In two parallel tracks, diploid microsporocytes and megasporocytes undergo meiosis. Haploid microspores develop by mitosis into pollen with two sperm nuclei. One surviving megaspore develops by mitosis into an embryo sac with an egg and two polar nuclei. Double fertilization produces a diploid embryo and triploid endosperm in the mature kernel. Growth by mitosis returns to the mature sporophyte. Anatomical stages and nuclei are schematic and not to scale. | Original editable vector construction. Source facts: genetics/LECT06/djot/assets/lect06c-meiosis/image_031.jpg; source consumer: lect06c-meiosis.djot, The life cycle of corn. Natural organ contours are newly constructed. Nuclear colors retain source fusion partners. Diagram schematic, not to scale. | text{font-family:"Atkinson Hyperlegible Next",sans-serif;fill:#213547;font-size:24px}
 .small{font-size:21px}.tiny{font-size:19px}.label{font-size:24px}.head{font-size:27px;font-weight:bold}
 .leader{fill:none;stroke:#526879;stroke-width:1.8;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round}
 .flow{fill:none;stroke:#526879;stroke-width:3;marker-end:url(#arrow)}
 .return{fill:none;stroke:#526879;stroke-width:4;marker-end:url(#large-arrow)}
 .cell{fill:#fff9ec;stroke:#7d6d51;stroke-width:2.5}
 .organ{stroke:#355936;stroke-width:2.5;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-linecap:round} | Meiosis | Mitosis | Schematic; not to scale | Tassel | Ear shoot | Mature sporophyte | (2n) | Microsporocyte | (2n) | Four microspores (n) | Microspore | (n) | Germinated | pollen grain | Two sperm | nuclei (n) | Megasporocyte | (2n) | Megaspores (n) | Surviving | megaspore | Mature | embryo sac | Polar nuclei (n) | Egg nucleus (n) | Fertilization | Endosperm | (3n) | Embryo | (2n) | Mature kernel | Endosperm (3n) | The endosperm (triploid) results | from the fusion of two haploid | maternal nuclei and one haploid | paternal nucleus. | Embryo (2n) | The embryo (diploid) results | from the fusion of one | haploid maternal nucleus | and one haploid paternal nucleus. | Growth by mitosis
